ProsperoSunshine: with address_family = both the IPv6 sockets take IPv4 too

"both" opens the RTSP acceptor and the video and audio sockets for IPv6 and binds them to "::". Linux and Windows let such
a socket take IPv4 as well unless told otherwise, so Sunshine never says so. FreeBSD doesn't (net.inet6.ip6.v6only is 1 by
default), and the PS5's system is built on it: there "both" would have meant IPv6 only for these three, while ENet's control
socket, which clears IPV6_V6ONLY itself, still took IPv4. With the HTTP servers IPv6 only as well, Moonlight over IPv4, the
LAN included, could no longer reach the host. net::take_ipv4_too clears the option between open and bind; a system that refuses
it leaves the socket IPv6 only, and the log says so (issue 64). The HTTP and HTTPS servers get the same in
Simple-Web-Server (patches/simple-web-server/0004).

--- a/src/network.h
+++ b/src/network.h
@@ -127,6 +127,24 @@
   std::string get_bind_address(af_e af);
 
   /**
+   * @brief ProsperoSunshine: lets a socket opened for IPv6 take IPv4 too, which is what address_family = both means.
+   * Linux and Windows do that unless told otherwise; FreeBSD, and so the PS5, keep an IPv6 socket to IPv6, and
+   * Moonlight over IPv4 could no longer reach the host. Call it between open and bind.
+   * @param socket An open acceptor or socket.
+   * @param af The family it was opened for; an IPv4 socket is left alone.
+   * @return false when the system refused: the socket then takes IPv6 only.
+   */
+  template<class Socket>
+  bool take_ipv4_too(Socket &socket, af_e af) {
+    if (af == IPV4) {
+      return true;
+    }
+    boost::system::error_code ec;
+    socket.set_option(boost::asio::ip::v6_only(false), ec);
+    return !ec;
+  }
+
+  /**
    * @brief Get the configured bind address formatted as a URL host.
    * @details IPv6 addresses are enclosed in brackets. An empty bind address is represented as `localhost`.
    * @return URL host for links to services bound by Sunshine.
--- a/src/rtsp.cpp
+++ b/src/rtsp.cpp
@@ -443,6 +443,9 @@
       if (ec) {
         return -1;
       }
+      if (!net::take_ipv4_too(acceptor, af)) {
+        BOOST_LOG(warning) << "The RTSP port takes IPv6 only: this system doesn't let an IPv6 socket take IPv4 too"sv;
+      }
 
       acceptor.set_option(boost::asio::socket_base::reuse_address {true});
 
--- a/src/stream.cpp
+++ b/src/stream.cpp
@@ -2128,6 +2128,9 @@
 
       return -1;
     }
+    if (!net::take_ipv4_too(ctx.video_sock, address_family)) {
+      BOOST_LOG(warning) << "The video and audio ports take IPv6 only: this system doesn't let an IPv6 socket take IPv4 too"sv;
+    }
 
     // Set video socket send buffer size (SO_SENDBUF) to 1MB
     try {
@@ -2157,6 +2160,7 @@
 
       return -1;
     }
+    net::take_ipv4_too(ctx.audio_sock, address_family);
 
     platf::trace_call("bind the audio port UDP " + std::to_string(audio_port));
     ctx.audio_sock.bind(udp::endpoint(bind_addr, audio_port), ec);
